      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this wonderful four-bedroom two-bathroom semi-detached family home sitting on an extra-large site to the market on the prestigious Mill Road, Saggart. This stunning property is situated in a prime location within walking distance of Rathcoole and Saggart Villages with their array of amenities. Avoca, local primary and secondary schools, The Luas and Rathcoole Park with its beautiful scenery and walking trails are but a few of the many attractions to this excellent location. \r\n\r\nBright, airy and most spacious internal living accommodation of C. 159 sqm briefly comprises of entrance hallway with ample storage, beautiful fully fitted kitchen, large living room with range, double bedroom, main family bathroom and separate laundry room which could be used as another bedroom if needed. On the first floor you have three spacious bedrooms and another main family bathroom. All bedrooms come with top-quality built-in wardrobes and bathroom suites are fully tiled. \r\n\r\nTo the rear of the property comes the real show piece of the home, an extra-large rear garden of the lowest maintenance with the use of block-built sheds that can be used for so many different purposes, rear gardens the size of this one doesn't exist anymore and the potential for further development here is endless. \r\n\r\nNo. 17 Mill Road, Saggart is undoubtably one of the best homes to come to the market in Saggart this year. It's in fantastic condition throughout having been lovingly maintained by its current owners with no expense spared when upgrading in recent years and we see this one being extremely popular among a wide range of buyers such as any growing family looking to settle roots in one of the most sought-after roads in all of Saggart. It boasts plenty of additional features such as large site, extra spacious living, gas fired central heating, double glazed windows and top-quality fixtures & fittings to name but a few. \r\n\r\nDo not miss this one; call Ray Cooke Auctioneers for further information or to arrange viewing! \r\n\r\nAdditional features; \r\n- BER - C \r\n- c. 159 sqm \r\n- 4 bed / 2 bath \r\n- Semi-detached family home \r\n- Extra-large site \r\n- Plenty of scope for further development \r\n- Gas fired central heating\r\n- Dual heating \r\n- Double glazed windows\r\n- Top quality blinds \r\n- Fantastic condition throughout\r\n- Tastefully decorated from top to bottom \r\n- Ample storage \r\n- Entrance hallway \r\n- Beautiful fully fitted kitchen\r\n- Large living room with range \r\n- Separate utility room \r\n- Landing leads to bedrooms \r\n- Four spacious bedrooms\r\n- Could be used as a 5-bed house \r\n- Built in wardrobes \r\n- Fully tiled bathrooms suites\r\n- Ensuite bathroom fully tiled\r\n- Ample parking to the front \r\n- Large rear garden \r\n- Block built units to the rear \r\n- Can be used for so many different purposes \r\n- Highly sought-after area\r\n- Bus routes on your doorstep \r\n- Within easy reach of Rathcoole and Saggart Village \r\n- Within easy reach of The M50 Motorway & The Luas \r\n- Ideal for growing families\r\n\r\nDirections - From Red Cow, proceed along Naas Road. Continue through the lights at Newlands Cross and then take the 4th exit for Rathcoole / Saggart. At the roundabout turn left and follow the road ahead. At the next roundabout take the first exit onto Mill Road where number 17 will be clearly sign posted on the left."
      },
